# SAFE-5c: line to append to box2's ~/.ssh/authorized_keys for the
# dedicated box1-agent key (a NEW keypair generated on box1 for this
# purpose only -- do not reuse any existing box1 key, so it can be
# revoked independently of anything else box1 does).
#
# This line is what makes the channel "forced": no matter what command
# box1's ssh client asks to run, sshd runs `command=` instead, and the
# no-* options strip every other thing SSH could otherwise be used for
# (port forwarding = a generic TCP proxy to anything on box2's network
# namespace, agent forwarding = box1 borrowing box2's other keys, pty/
# X11 = an interactive shell or GUI channel). What's left is exactly:
# "run gateway-relay.sh, feed it box1's stdin, return its stdout" -- a
# fixed program box2 controls, not an arbitrary command.
#
# STATUS: NOT installed (needs box1's pubkey, which we don't have -- see
# state/reports/2026-09-14-safe5c-box2-half.md). Template below has a
# placeholder for the real box1 pubkey.

command="/home/cm/projects/alice-aegis/demo/agent-trace/gateway/deploy/inter-box/gateway-relay.sh",no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,no-pty,restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...REPLACE-WITH-BOX1-AGENT-PUBKEY... cm-box1-agent-relay-only
